FILE K11/source/docs/architecture-overview.md
180: ###	Use Case Create Registration Token
181: It is important to note, that only one Registration Token will be generated for a specific GUID or teleTAN. The use case generates Registration Tokens from hashed GUIDs xor teleTANs. This is a measure to increase data privacy.
182: 
183: API Endpoint:
184: -	Method: POST /registrationToken
185: Body: { 
186: "key": "<< key >>",
187: "keyType": “teleTAN||hashedGUID” 
188: }
189: -	Authentication: none
190: 
191: Steps
192: 1.	Verify whether a registration token with the provided GUID or teleTAN already exists, if yes return error
193: 1.  If a teleTAN is used for creation, verify teleTAN.
194: 	1. If verification fails, return HTTP 400
195: 2.	Create Registration Token
196: 3.	Store entity AppSession, with hashed Registration Token. If available store hashed GUID, if available store hashed teleTAN. Mark AppSession.sourceOfTrust
197: 4.	Return Registration Token.sourceOfTrust depending on which source (hashed GUID or teleTAN) was provided
198: 5.	If teleTAN was provided mark teleTAN as redeemed
